.TH UC2 1 "October 2026" "uc2 3.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
uc2 \- UltraCompressor II archiver revival
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B uc2
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIarchive.uc2\fR [\fIFILES...\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B uc2
is a cross-platform revival of UltraCompressor II, the DOS-era archiver by Nico de Vries (1992-1996), rewritten as a modern, portable C99 tool with backward compatibility by Evgeny Valetov.
It supports content-defined chunking (CDC), master block deduplication, rANS entropy coding, and BLAKE3 integrity verification.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-w
Create archive.
.TP
.B \-l
List archive contents.
.TP
.B \-t
Test archive integrity.
.TP
.BI \-L " level"
Compression level: 2=Fast, 3=Normal, 4=Tight (default), 5=Ultra (levels 2-5 use Huffman and are compatible with DOS UC2 Pro); 6-9 use modern rANS entropy coding.
.TP
.BI \-d " path"
Destination directory to extract to.
.TP
.B \-f
Force overwrite of existing files during extraction.
.TP
.B \-p
Extract files to standard output.
.TP
.B \-q
Quiet mode (suppress status messages).
.TP
.B \-a
Include all file versions.
.TP
.B \-D
Do not set time and permissions of directories (-DD also skips file metadata).
.TP
.B \-T
Tab-separated output for listing archive contents.
.TP
.B \-B
Benchmark all compression methods on input files.
.SH AUTHOR
Original UC2 by Nico de Vries (1992-1996).
Revival implementation by Evgeny Valetov.
Packaged for Trinity Desktop Environment (TDE) / TdeZip companion tools.
